From fe299de6458a3dd61fac4e6e01e55e9de2e07217 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:49:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wallguard: the list compiler, the updater and rstore

wallguardc compiles hosts, plain-domain and ||name^ lists plus My rules into the
table dnsmasq maps (tmp + fsync + rename; at most 1,000,000 names, earlier
lists and the operator's rules win), explains a name per profile and resolves
the safe-search enforcement hosts. wallguard.sh fetches the subscribed lists
(https only, 32 MB each, the previous copy kept on a failure), builds, folds the
blocked-lookup records into counters (200 busiest names and devices) and prints
the page's status. A boot before the WAN is up leaves a pending mark so the
lists are fetched again at WAN up and every 10 min; the lists held in RAM stay
under 96 MB together and none is fetched under 160 MB of free memory; history
to USB is queued for one detached writer so the page never waits on the disk.
rstore is the shell's no-follow store tool. services.txt: the blocked-services
catalog. The router Makefile also builds rednsd and dreadwatch and passes the
Samba quota setting.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
